    {
      "id": "lp_scroll",
      "type": "JavaScriptFunction",
      "label": "Changing step starts at the top",
      "x": 1100,
      "y": 400,
      "parameters": {
        "functionScript": "if (typeof window !== 'undefined') window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });\n"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "comment": "The one thing a node cannot do. Runs only on the signal."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lp_strings",
      "type": "/Data/Strings",
      "label": "Every word on screen",
      "x": 760,
      "y": 40,
      "metadata": {
        "comment": "One instance per page. Its `copy` output is the whole bundle; Logic/Sections for step puts it on every row, and the For Each maps it onto Section row's Copy input by name. Delete this node and the lesson still renders — in the English the kit ships (TASK-L160). A lesson is the learner's surface. When a coach can read one, this is the line that changes — one word, in the instance, rather than a flag threaded through the kit (TASK-L163 §3)."
      },
      "parameters": {
        "audience": "learner"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "seo_lp_page",
      "type": "JavaScriptFunction",
      "label": "Set the browser tab",
      "x": 1400,
      "y": 1430,
      "parameters": {
        "functionScript": "// The page title is the browser TAB, and it is the one learner-facing string a\n// Translation node cannot reach: `Page.title` is read off the node's PARAMETERS at\n// export time into the router index (utils/exporter/router.ts), and the Router hands\n// that to Noodl.SEO.setTitle on mount. A connection to the port is silently ignored —\n// measured, TASK-L161 §1: with the parameter removed and a Translation wired, the tab\n// read \"Home\", the component name.\n//\n// So the parameter stays as the BUILD-TIME FALLBACK (the router index needs it, and it\n// is what the tab shows for the instant before this runs), and the translated value\n// overrides it here. Same shape as the kit's built-in English: a fallback is not a\n// second owner.\nconst t = Inputs.title;\nif (typeof t === 'string' && t !== '' && typeof Noodl !== 'undefined' && Noodl.SEO) {\n  Noodl.SEO.setTitle(t);\n}\n"
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "in-title",
          "plug": "input",
          "type": "string",
          "displayName": "title",
          "group": "Inputs"
        }
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "comment": "Why a JavaScript node and not a wire to Page.title: the port is build-time. See the script."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lp_lang_var",
      "type": "Variable",
      "label": "language — from the one owner in App",
      "x": 1120,
      "y": 40,
      "parameters": {
        "name": "language"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "comment": "A TRANSPORT, NEVER A SECOND DECISION. `Data/Strings` is instantiated once per surface that needs the kit's copy object, and a component cannot wire across to another, so the resolved language is broadcast through this named Variable. The one OWNER is still the `i18next` node in App: this node only carries its answer. Every `/Data/Strings` instance in the project learns the language exactly this way — TASK-L162 §2."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lp_url",
      "type": "PageInputs",
      "label": "Whose, which step, draft or published — ?learner=&concept=&which=",
      "x": 800,
      "y": 40,
      "parameters": {
        "queryParams": "learner,concept,which"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "comment": "The fixture was one lesson and the page never had to say which. The backend holds one per concept, so every link to this page passes the concept it names: the up-next card and the dossier's lesson link on /course (TASK-L171 §0b). A query parameter rather than a path one so /lesson with no concept is still a page, not a 404."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lp_state",
      "type": "JavaScriptFunction",
      "label": "Something to preview, or not",
      "x": 1100,
      "y": 160,
      "parameters": {
        "functionScript": "/*\n * WRITTEN, OR NOT YET (TASK-L171 §0b). `found` is undefined until the answer\n * arrives, so neither state draws while the lesson is on its way — the page does\n * not flash \"not written yet\" at somebody whose lesson is one request away.\n */\nOutputs.hasLesson = Inputs.found === true;\nOutputs.notWritten = Inputs.found === false;\n"
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "in-found",
          "displayName": "found",
          "plug": "input",
          "type": "*",
          "group": "Inputs"
        },
        {
          "name": "out-hasLesson",
          "displayName": "hasLesson",
          "plug": "output",
          "type": "*",
          "group": "Outputs"
        },
        {
          "name": "out-notWritten",
          "displayName": "notWritten",
          "plug": "output",
          "type": "*",
          "group": "Outputs"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lp_none",
      "type": "Group",
      "label": "Not written yet",
      "x": 220,
      "y": 1180,
      "parent": "lp_shell",
      "parameters": {
        "width": {
          "value": 100,
          "unit": "%"
        },
        "sizeMode": "contentHeight",
        "flexDirection": "column",
        "alignItems": "flex-start",
        "rowGap": "var(--space-4)",
        "mounted": false
      },
      "metadata": {
        "comment": "Sprint 49 decision 7 promised this: Sam's next step has no lesson written for it until the engine sprint, and the up-next card opens it. MOUNTED, never visible (L157): visibility keeps the space. No colour of its own and no warning tone — a lesson not written yet is not something the learner did wrong."
      },
      "children": [
        "lp_none_eyebrow",
        "lp_none_title",
        "lp_none_body"
      ]
